# Merge quality gate (mandatory)

**Never merge a PR to `main` if any required check is red or pending.**
**Never `git push origin main` to bypass that gate.**

## Before every merge

Run on the PR branch:

```bash
gh pr checks <number>
npm run sonar:gate -- --status --pr <number>
```

Do not merge until **all** of the following are `pass` (or `skipping` when expected):

| Check | When required |
|---|---|
| **SonarCloud Code Analysis** | Always (GitHub App decoration) |
| **SonarCloud quality gate** | Always (workflow waits on the App check and fails closed) |
| **Lint and build** | Web paths changed (see `web-quality.yml`) |
| **Build debug APK** | Android paths changed (see `android-native.yml`) |

If SonarCloud shows `fail`, **stop**. Fix the Sonar issues on the branch, push, wait for green, then merge. Do not bypass.

## Why

1. PR #121 was merged with Sonar red (`Math.random()` in `lib/boss-api-handlers.js`).
2. Polyglot CI was **pushed straight to `main`** (no PR). Automatic Analysis then scored new Python/Actions/Ruby files and flipped `main` from Green to Red (`new_reliability_rating` + `new_security_rating`).

Rules-only enforcement is not enough. The **SonarCloud quality gate** workflow fails CI when the App check is red. The owner still must make that check **required** in GitHub (agents cannot set branch protection).

## GitHub branch protection (human setup)

Owner: GitHub → Settings → Branches → rule for `main`:

- Require a pull request before merging
- Do not allow bypassing the above settings
- Require status checks to pass:
  - `SonarCloud Code Analysis`
  - `SonarCloud quality gate`
- Do **not** require path-filtered jobs (`Lint and build`, `Build debug APK`) on every PR — they will not run on unrelated diffs and will stick the merge box.

Until branch protection is enabled, agents must self-enforce via `gh pr checks`.
